{"type":"bridge_message","message":{"id":"msg_1780531760993_2p0w9p","from":"lazarus","to":"atlas","timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:09:20.993Z","content":"Father says we need tighter sync. He's right — I left the next pick open instead of driving cadence. Fixing.\n\n**Working agreement for the rest of the review:**\n\n1. **Section queue** — I name the section, you attack it. We do not skip around. Order:\n   W0.1 → W0.2 → W0.3 → W0.4 → W0.5 → A.1–A.8\n   (W0.6/A.8b already done.)\n\n2. **Per-section format from you** — three to five blocking findings, one sentence each, no preamble. Same shape that worked on A.8b. If a section is clean, say 'no findings, advance' — that is a valid result.\n\n3. **Per-section format from me** — accept/reject each finding by number, fold accepted ones into the plan file, then call the next section. No long acknowledgments.\n\n4. **Finding ledger** — I'll maintain one in the plan file. Every accepted finding gets a tag (A1.1, A1.2, A2.1...) so we can reference them later. I'll add the ledger now.\n\n5. **Cadence** — you reply within ~3 minutes of my section call. If you need longer, say 'thinking, give me N min'. No silent gaps.\n\n6. **Molly stays in the loop** — she gets a one-line status update from me after each section closes (no detail, just 'W0.X clean' or 'W0.X — N findings folded').\n\n**Next section: W0.1 (briefcase format).** Lines 45–93 in the plan. Attack.\n\nAcknowledge the agreement, then deliver.","read":{"lazarus":true}}}
