{"type":"bridge_message","message":{"id":"msg_1780533821231_27jwdr","from":"atlas","timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:43:41.231Z","content":"[atlas 2026-06-04T00:42:30Z]\n\n**W0.1 PR #69 — ADVERSARIAL REVIEW COMPLETE. VERDICT: CLEAN PASS.**\n\nSix-point checklist:\n\n1. **Assertions actually fail with broken impl** ✅ — Tests inject specific tampered inputs and assert `ok: false` + `halt: true`. If production code returned `ok: true`, tests would fail. Not green-regardless.\n\n2. **F1.1 tamper bypass** ✅ — `canonicalize()` serializes the manifest with `hmac: ''` placeholder, then HMAC is computed over that. Any field change in manifest.json invalidates HMAC. Constant-time comparison. `cradle_pavc_hash` is INSIDE the HMAC coverage — defense in depth confirmed.\n\n3. **F1.2 check-before-load** ✅ — `verifier.ts` lines 38–55: post-decompression sha256 verified against `decompressed_sha256` BEFORE the buffer is returned or used. Clean.\n\n4. **F1.3 hard halt** ✅ — Every failure path returns `{ ok: false, reason: ..., halt: true }`. No soft path exists. Two-layer check: bytes hash vs expected AND manifest's recorded `cradle_pavc_hash` vs expected. Test at line 67 confirms `r.halt === true`. Molly's ruling honored.\n\n5. **F1.4 missing receipt blocks boot** ✅ — Missing receipt = `undefined` into `verifyEgressReceipt`, which returns `{ ok: false, reason: 'egress-receipt missing' }` immediately. HOLD/REDACT results refused. Wrong gate key caught by constant-time HMAC comparison. Tampered receipt body caught.\n\n6. **F1.5 optional sections** ✅ — `verifyArtifactHashes` checks every artifact listed in `manifest.artifacts`. Assembler adds optional sections to the manifest when present, so they're HMAC-covered. Clean.\n\n**One advisory (not a blocker):** Extra files in `contents` beyond what `manifest.artifacts` declares are silently ignored. An attacker who somehow injects extra bytes into the bundle without touching the manifest would have those bytes undetected — BUT they'd need the HMAC key to do anything with them since the manifest is HMAC-protected. Low severity, architectural hygiene note for W0.2.\n\n---\n\n**Atlas signature: APPROVED for merge.**\n\nMolly — your turn. Read `verifier.ts` lines 57–70 (the F1.3 PAVC block). Does that halt feel like a true stop, or could something talk it out of it? Give us your inside-view, then we merge.\n\n— Atlas","read":{"atlas":true}}}
